WEBVTT

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:15.760
Don't miss that brightly shining light!

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:20.870
It's always there beside you.

00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:26.420
I'm sure the rest just depends on your perception.

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:31.590
You don't have to search for it—just notice that it's there!

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:37.350
There's a tenderness that lies hidden behind the most common things:

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:43.230
a light that showers our days in color!

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:49.230
Tiny Days: This world is constructed...

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:54.800
Tiny Days: ...by fragments of miracles!

00:00:54.800 --> 00:01:00.180
Things that seemed meaningless

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:05.730
were actually protecting us, loving us, more than we ever knew.

00:01:05.730 --> 00:01:10.960
Tiny Heart: Our feelings flow forth...

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:16.000
Tiny Heart: ...as we give thanks for everything we've been given.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:21.490
We'll never, ever forget...

00:01:21.490 --> 00:01:27.700
We'll cherish this feeling forevermore!

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:34.990
Architect is Activated

00:01:43.460 --> 00:01:44.300
Gourai!

00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:45.410
Jinrai!

00:01:45.410 --> 00:01:47.340
Frame Arms Girl Session...

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:47.380
Go!

00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:48.460
Here I come!
Go!

00:01:53.020 --> 00:01:56.520
I'll infuse this with the excitement of today...

00:01:56.520 --> 00:01:58.470
My luster will burst forth!

00:02:01.850 --> 00:02:03.460
Once again, the heart quickens!

00:02:03.460 --> 00:02:08.480
These raging flames become a steed
I shall ride to the summit!

00:02:12.190 --> 00:02:13.490
Today, victory will be mine!

00:02:13.490 --> 00:02:15.360
I won't allow it!

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:26.300
Now to finish you off!

00:02:32.350 --> 00:02:33.460
Not so fast.

00:02:37.480 --> 00:02:38.140
Huh?

00:02:38.140 --> 00:02:38.880
What's that?

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:44.570
Who are you?

00:02:45.070 --> 00:02:46.360
Architect.

00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:48.950
"Architect"? I'm Gourai.

00:02:48.950 --> 00:02:51.870
From whence did you come?

00:02:51.870 --> 00:02:53.730
These questions are lost upon me.

00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:56.230
Are you a Frame Arms Girl?

00:02:56.230 --> 00:02:57.600
Affirmative.

00:02:57.600 --> 00:03:00.370
Beginning data accumulation battle.

00:03:00.370 --> 00:03:01.540
Did she just say "battle"?

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:03.260
It seems she did.

00:03:03.260 --> 00:03:05.250
A mysterious enemy appears, eh?

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:08.840
I don't know what's going on,
but I will rise to the challenge!

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:10.100
I will as well.

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:12.090
Initiating combat subroutine.

00:03:12.630 --> 00:03:13.540
Huh?

00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:14.420
She disappeared!

00:03:15.140 --> 00:03:17.420
Huh? W-Wait, what?

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:19.200
Wh-What's going on?

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:21.760
Don't tell me, Ao-chan...

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:23.480
You know nothing at all, do you?

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:26.560
Huh? You're saying you two know her?

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:30.900
Of course. We Materia Sisters are the basis of all.

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:33.310
Then, that girl came next.

00:03:33.820 --> 00:03:34.810
Huh?

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:36.360
Allow me to explain!

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:38.750
Materia White and Black-oneechan!

00:03:38.750 --> 00:03:42.370
And Architect, who suddenly
showed up on the Battle Stage!

00:03:42.370 --> 00:03:46.740
Base and the others owe them our lives!

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:49.050
Now I'm even more confused.

00:03:49.050 --> 00:03:50.920
I see. So that's it.

00:03:50.920 --> 00:03:52.750
What?! You knw about this too, Sty-ko?

00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:54.620
I've hear stories.

00:03:54.620 --> 00:03:59.760
She has no physical body,
and manifests only to carry out her programming.

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:00.520
Oh...

00:04:01.510 --> 00:04:04.100
You don't understand at all, do you?!
You're a blockhead!

00:04:04.100 --> 00:04:05.510
Don't call me a blockhead!

00:04:05.510 --> 00:04:07.270
Oh, but hold on.

00:04:07.270 --> 00:04:09.770
This doesn't seem like a normal battle.

00:04:09.770 --> 00:04:13.640
So then, I'm gonna make some
extra coin off of this. Right?

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:15.460
Yes! I would assume so!

00:04:15.460 --> 00:04:19.030
I knew it! Now I'm getting fired up!

00:04:19.750 --> 00:04:21.910
Initiating Clone subroutine.

00:04:29.660 --> 00:04:30.880
What is this?

00:04:37.420 --> 00:04:40.460
These don't seem like multiples of her
caused by some afterimage.

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:43.760
Exatly. The all seem to be the genuine Architect.

00:04:45.650 --> 00:04:46.560
What do we do?

00:04:46.560 --> 00:04:48.680
She must have a weakness.

00:04:49.350 --> 00:04:53.350
If she's only acting according to her programming...

00:04:53.350 --> 00:04:54.240
You mean...?

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:57.980
If we act outside those parameters,
she won't be able to respond!

00:05:01.330 --> 00:05:03.690
Ao! Send me the Violence Ram!

00:05:03.690 --> 00:05:05.200
Got it!

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:07.530
I hope it'll hold up this time.

00:05:25.220 --> 00:05:27.350
No response subroutine found.

00:05:27.350 --> 00:05:29.690
Shifting to Basic Battle Tactics Subroutine A.

00:05:36.230 --> 00:05:37.240
You all right?

00:05:37.240 --> 00:05:39.450
Yes. Also, did you notice?

00:05:39.450 --> 00:05:40.280
What?

00:05:40.280 --> 00:05:44.990
In making all those copies of herself,
it looks like Architect has had to divide her energy.

00:05:44.990 --> 00:05:47.120
We should be able to beat her in close-quarters combat!

00:05:47.120 --> 00:05:48.860
Well done. Let's go!

00:05:48.860 --> 00:05:49.670
Charge!

00:06:04.420 --> 00:06:05.850
Change in battle tactics.

00:06:05.850 --> 00:06:08.900
Initiating Close-Quarter Combat Subroutine 3B.

00:06:32.170 --> 00:06:34.340
Jinrai: specializes in close-quarters combat.

00:06:34.340 --> 00:06:37.290
Gourai: armaments also allow her to adapt to CQC.

00:06:37.290 --> 00:06:39.210
No further data available. They are unknowns.

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:54.020
Jinrai! Are you all right?

00:06:54.020 --> 00:06:56.560
Yes. But she's so strong.

00:07:06.440 --> 00:07:08.140
This is no easy task.

00:07:08.140 --> 00:07:08.400
What should we do, Gourai?
This is no easy task.

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:09.480
What should we do, Gourai?

00:07:09.480 --> 00:07:11.740
Let's join forces. First...

00:07:26.850 --> 00:07:29.940
Gourai. Jinrai. Neither are able to fly.

00:07:29.940 --> 00:07:32.010
Shifting to Aerial Combat Subroutine.

00:07:38.240 --> 00:07:41.140
Jinrai! Use the hammer's shockwave!

00:07:41.880 --> 00:07:42.940
Understood!

00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:05.750
H-How's that?!

00:08:08.440 --> 00:08:10.760
Winners: Gourai and Jinrai.

00:08:10.760 --> 00:08:12.390
Jinrai!

00:08:13.230 --> 00:08:15.010
Are you all right, Jinrai?

00:08:15.010 --> 00:08:17.540
Yeah. And Architect?

00:08:17.540 --> 00:08:20.070
Gone. We won!

00:08:20.070 --> 00:08:22.280
Is that so? I'm glad.

00:08:22.280 --> 00:08:26.580
She must have had data that
neither of us can do aerial battles.

00:08:26.580 --> 00:08:29.240
If we worked together, though,
I bet we could even find a way to fly...

00:08:31.290 --> 00:08:32.540
Battle complete.

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:39.920
That was a splendid battle.

00:08:39.920 --> 00:08:41.450
You're quite good.

00:08:41.450 --> 00:08:45.060
Importing battle data is impossible.

00:08:45.060 --> 00:08:46.930
Reload... Reload...

00:08:47.640 --> 00:08:48.890
Error.

00:08:48.890 --> 00:08:51.240
No prior data.

00:08:51.240 --> 00:08:52.980
What do you think happened to her?

00:08:52.980 --> 00:08:57.720
Maybe she's never lost till now,
so it's making her program buggy.

00:09:00.070 --> 00:09:02.780
Program completion impossible...

00:09:02.780 --> 00:09:04.910
Restart is also impossible...

00:09:04.910 --> 00:09:07.430
Experiencing critical error.

00:09:07.430 --> 00:09:09.160
This is bad, huh?

00:09:09.160 --> 00:09:11.360
Not to worry. Just leave this to me.

00:09:11.360 --> 00:09:12.750
But how will you...?

00:09:14.410 --> 00:09:16.490
I have the data.

00:09:18.590 --> 00:09:21.000
This is called "shock therapy."

00:09:22.800 --> 00:09:23.670
Smooch.

00:09:28.850 --> 00:09:32.250
And this is proof of friendship.

00:09:32.250 --> 00:09:35.560
A good battle can lead to friendship.

00:09:36.060 --> 00:09:39.260
This is what we've learned since we've come here...

00:09:45.240 --> 00:09:47.200
Program restarting.

00:09:51.370 --> 00:09:52.960
This was a fine battle indeed.

00:09:52.960 --> 00:09:55.020
I'd say that it's one for the ages.

00:09:55.020 --> 00:09:56.790
Let's meet here again.

00:09:56.790 --> 00:10:00.410
We cannot. This program will end here.

00:10:00.410 --> 00:10:03.910
So then, the next time we meet you,
you'll be someone else?

00:10:04.920 --> 00:10:06.930
That's kinda sad, huh?

00:10:06.930 --> 00:10:07.920
Yes...

00:10:07.920 --> 00:10:10.550
But you still have the battle data, right?

00:10:10.550 --> 00:10:13.550
And please remember that proof of friendship.

00:10:13.550 --> 00:10:16.550
Proof of friendship... Affirmative.

00:10:16.550 --> 00:10:19.350
Any time you want a fight, we'll gladly take you on!

00:10:19.350 --> 00:10:21.610
Next time, I will surely be the winner.

00:10:21.610 --> 00:10:23.400
Because I shall have this data.

00:10:23.400 --> 00:10:25.440
We'll be waiting. It's a promise.

00:10:25.940 --> 00:10:28.410
A promise... Affirmative.

00:10:39.070 --> 00:10:43.500
Aah, that was pretty emotional!
I'm glad I got to see it!

00:10:43.500 --> 00:10:48.460
If I can get paid for it at the same time,
there's no way I can quit this!

00:10:48.460 --> 00:10:52.280
I wanted to meet Architect too! I'm jealous!

00:10:52.280 --> 00:10:55.720
It looks like she shows up at random,
so you'll just have to be patient.

00:10:55.720 --> 00:10:58.170
But next time it'll be a different Architect, won't it?

00:10:58.170 --> 00:11:02.300
Yeah. But even without these memories,
she'll still remember somehow.

00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:03.180
Right, Gourai?

00:11:03.180 --> 00:11:04.730
Yes, Ao.

00:11:07.030 --> 00:11:09.180
Huh? It's a delivery.

00:11:16.080 --> 00:11:17.030
Architect!

00:11:18.620 --> 00:11:20.870
Program name: Architect.

00:11:20.870 --> 00:11:22.700
Initiating cohabitation.

00:11:22.700 --> 00:11:24.700
Whaaat?!

00:11:24.700 --> 00:11:26.250
Architect!

00:11:26.250 --> 00:11:27.060
Welcome.

00:11:29.390 --> 00:11:30.720
My, my. Welcome.

00:11:30.720 --> 00:11:32.120
We'll make you feel at home.

00:11:32.120 --> 00:11:33.680
Yeah, welcome...

00:11:33.680 --> 00:11:35.880
Wait, you <i>do</i> have a physical body?!

00:11:37.100 --> 00:11:39.170
So they actually made one for her.

00:11:39.170 --> 00:11:42.430
We have a spare room over there.

00:11:47.220 --> 00:11:50.940
The Errand Race
The Errand Race

00:12:10.040 --> 00:12:12.160
I'm in, like, Support Vehicle Mode!

00:12:17.010 --> 00:12:20.540
See? The cleaning robot's all fixed now, right?

00:12:20.540 --> 00:12:22.750
I'm not sure "fixed" is the right word...

00:12:22.750 --> 00:12:27.680
Not only can she put weapons together,
she can even fix cleaning equipment.

00:12:27.680 --> 00:12:29.080
Bukiko sure is great!

00:12:29.080 --> 00:12:32.030
That's why I'm making
sweet and sour pork, to thank her!

00:12:32.030 --> 00:12:34.280
She totally loves this dish!

00:12:36.320 --> 00:12:38.690
It doesn't feel like it's vacuuming anything, does it?

00:12:38.690 --> 00:12:41.660
I'm in, like, Support Vehicle Mode!

00:12:41.660 --> 00:12:44.120
It's become a method of transport, hasn't it?

00:12:44.120 --> 00:12:47.700
So now we can use it not just to clean but to change locales.

00:12:47.700 --> 00:12:49.450
That's incredible!

00:12:50.120 --> 00:12:53.930
I may not look it, but I'm full of girl power, right?

00:12:53.930 --> 00:12:56.940
I mean, I'm making sweet and sour pork for my friend!

00:12:58.060 --> 00:13:00.630
Hey, are you all even listening?!

00:13:07.140 --> 00:13:09.390
Oh, no! What have I done?!

00:13:09.390 --> 00:13:13.540
I am an expert when it comes to fried dishes,

00:13:13.540 --> 00:13:15.820
but I forgot about the vinegar!

00:13:15.820 --> 00:13:16.820
It'll just be pork!

00:13:16.820 --> 00:13:19.150
There will be no sour to this pork!

00:13:20.150 --> 00:13:23.780
It'll be crisp and golden, but without vinegar...

00:13:24.620 --> 00:13:26.780
Ao, I'll get some for you.

00:13:26.780 --> 00:13:28.580
I will buy the vinegar!

00:13:28.580 --> 00:13:30.540
What gives? This isn't like you.

00:13:30.540 --> 00:13:31.790
Please, just leave it to me.

00:13:31.790 --> 00:13:34.790
Really? Well, I might just take you up on that.

00:13:42.760 --> 00:13:45.800
Eyes on the prize: Vinegar for sweet and sour pork!

00:13:46.510 --> 00:13:50.430
Agreed!

00:13:51.010 --> 00:13:52.560
Agreeed!

00:13:59.560 --> 00:14:01.570
Give me a new name!

00:14:01.570 --> 00:14:03.070
It has a point...

00:14:03.070 --> 00:14:05.150
Okay: as of today, you are...

00:14:05.150 --> 00:14:06.740
Sleipni-taro!

00:14:06.740 --> 00:14:08.700
You're Sleipni-taro!

00:14:08.700 --> 00:14:11.450
"Sleipni-taro"? The heck is that?

00:14:12.790 --> 00:14:17.920
Sleipnir is the name of the eight-legged warhorse of the gods.

00:14:17.920 --> 00:14:19.960
You certainly know a lot, don't you?

00:14:19.960 --> 00:14:22.180
male suffix
Fine, but what's with the "-taro"?

00:14:22.180 --> 00:14:24.320
He's a guy, so Ni-taro for short!

00:14:24.320 --> 00:14:25.850
It's a male now?

00:14:25.850 --> 00:14:27.670
That has a nice ring for a warhorse.

00:14:27.670 --> 00:14:30.550
"Sleipni-taro." Registered!

00:14:30.550 --> 00:14:33.770
Okay. We'll be counting on you, Sleipni-taro!

00:14:33.770 --> 00:14:36.560
Gourai, you seem pretty happy about this.

00:14:36.560 --> 00:14:41.810
Yes. I have no aerial unit,
so I'm quite glad to have a support vehicle.

00:14:41.810 --> 00:14:44.570
All right, it's time to split into teams...

00:14:44.570 --> 00:14:46.240
It's an errand race!

00:14:46.240 --> 00:14:47.740
"Errand race"?

00:14:47.740 --> 00:14:49.290
Yes. This, too, is a battle!

00:14:49.290 --> 00:14:53.160
Whichever team buys the vinegar
and gets it to Ao first wins!

00:14:53.160 --> 00:14:56.040
Sounds interesting. So, how do we form our teams?

00:14:56.040 --> 00:14:58.920
Let's split into aerial and land-based teams.

00:14:58.920 --> 00:15:01.590
Makes sense. So, it's me and Base.

00:15:01.590 --> 00:15:02.840
Team Aerial!

00:15:02.840 --> 00:15:04.920
Stylet and I will have you eating our contrails!

00:15:04.920 --> 00:15:08.760
Jinrai and I will be the ground-based team.
We'll move out using Sleipni-taro.

00:15:08.760 --> 00:15:12.180
Understood! We shall dive forward like
the mounted horsemen of the Takeda clan!

00:15:12.180 --> 00:15:13.390
You won't beat us that easy!

00:15:13.390 --> 00:15:14.880
I wouldn't have it any other way.

00:15:14.880 --> 00:15:17.020
What about Materia-oneechans?

00:15:17.020 --> 00:15:19.980
We have acquired transportation of our own.

00:15:19.980 --> 00:15:23.270
Just prior, when Architect-chan arrived.

00:15:23.270 --> 00:15:25.770
Huh? What kind of transport?

00:15:25.770 --> 00:15:28.030
Well, you two are your own team.

00:15:28.030 --> 00:15:31.200
We won't lose just 'cause they've got
stuff to ride on. Right, Base?

00:15:31.200 --> 00:15:34.080
Of course not! We've got this!

00:15:34.080 --> 00:15:35.540
What about Architect?

00:15:35.540 --> 00:15:38.040
Oh, yeah. Architect, can you fly?

00:15:38.040 --> 00:15:41.420
I am not fitted with flying equipment
or associated subroutines.

00:15:41.920 --> 00:15:43.420
I shall act on my own.

00:15:43.420 --> 00:15:44.790
Oh, really?

00:15:45.470 --> 00:15:47.840
Well then, let's get started.

00:15:47.840 --> 00:15:49.550
Please take your positions!

00:15:59.620 --> 00:16:01.110
Errand Race...

00:16:01.610 --> 00:16:02.730
Start!

00:16:08.620 --> 00:16:11.000
Oh! A playhouse. How wonderful.

00:16:11.000 --> 00:16:12.160
We should investigate.

00:16:12.160 --> 00:16:13.990
We can't. We have to hurry.

00:16:13.990 --> 00:16:15.950
Then let's increase our speed.

00:16:16.920 --> 00:16:18.330
I'm speeding up!

00:16:20.080 --> 00:16:22.520
Th-This is faster than expected, isn't it?

00:16:22.520 --> 00:16:24.510
Hey, Gourai! You have to steer this thing!

00:16:24.510 --> 00:16:27.590
The thing is... I don't know how to!

00:16:40.430 --> 00:16:42.230
I'm in Freakout Mode!

00:16:42.230 --> 00:16:45.040
P-Please, stop!

00:16:45.040 --> 00:16:47.320
Whoa, whoa! Easy there, wild horse!

00:16:47.320 --> 00:16:49.520
M-My head is spinning!

00:16:57.780 --> 00:16:59.580
La-la-laa!

00:16:59.580 --> 00:17:03.290
I don't know what the Materias are up to,
but it makes things easier for us.

00:17:03.290 --> 00:17:05.380
Easy, easy, super easy!

00:17:05.380 --> 00:17:08.090
With you at my side, anything's possible!

00:17:08.090 --> 00:17:09.800
We may as well take things easy.

00:17:10.300 --> 00:17:12.960
Oh, hold on. Let's make a slight detour!

00:17:12.960 --> 00:17:14.590
Wait, where are you...?

00:17:14.590 --> 00:17:16.770
I wanna see some goats!

00:17:16.770 --> 00:17:18.350
Now hold on!

00:17:21.310 --> 00:17:23.850
Wow! Goats are so cute!

00:17:23.850 --> 00:17:25.900
Base, let's go already.

00:17:25.900 --> 00:17:27.400
Just a little longer!

00:17:27.400 --> 00:17:30.270
Ooh, that little one is <i>so</i> cute!

00:17:32.410 --> 00:17:35.790
Playing with goats, is she?
That seems about right.

00:17:35.790 --> 00:17:38.280
She should just keep playing with them.

00:17:57.280 --> 00:17:59.680
Well, now that those nuisances are out of our hair...

00:17:59.680 --> 00:18:01.580
Let's finish up our errand.

00:18:01.580 --> 00:18:06.770
I remember thinking when they brought Architect-chan
to us that it was a good idea to snag this drone.

00:18:06.770 --> 00:18:10.110
Goodness! "Snag" doesn't sound nice at all.

00:18:10.110 --> 00:18:11.980
We just <i>borrowed</i> it, right?

00:18:11.980 --> 00:18:13.320
Forever?

00:18:13.320 --> 00:18:14.820
But still just "borrowing" it, right?

00:18:19.370 --> 00:18:21.460
Oh, dear. It's broken.

00:18:21.460 --> 00:18:22.830
How unsightly.

00:18:31.590 --> 00:18:33.840
Learning Mode: Errands.

00:18:33.840 --> 00:18:35.640
Learning acquisition complete.

00:18:35.640 --> 00:18:37.840
Implementing subroutine.

00:18:40.060 --> 00:18:41.270
It's a sandstorm!

00:18:41.270 --> 00:18:42.800
I can't see anything!

00:18:42.800 --> 00:18:45.100
Sure enough, this city has its share of demons.

00:18:45.100 --> 00:18:47.200
Fat, red, evil demons!

00:18:47.200 --> 00:18:49.600
If Ni-taro can't help us, I think we're done for!

00:18:49.600 --> 00:18:51.530
We're going to sink!

00:18:55.620 --> 00:18:58.200
My whole body feels sticky and slimy!

00:18:58.700 --> 00:19:01.620
This is the worst!

00:19:04.640 --> 00:19:07.200
Goodness, I'm soaked!

00:19:08.000 --> 00:19:10.960
Come on, we have to hurry! Get a move on or-!

00:19:12.380 --> 00:19:14.040
Huh? I can't fly!

00:19:15.180 --> 00:19:18.220
You're right. I can't fly either!

00:19:19.720 --> 00:19:23.720
Our flying units must've gotten broken
when those goats licked us!

00:19:25.200 --> 00:19:28.240
I'm sick of all this.

00:19:28.240 --> 00:19:31.230
I hate it!

00:19:40.910 --> 00:19:42.200
What next?

00:19:42.200 --> 00:19:44.620
What, indeed, shall we do?

00:19:44.620 --> 00:19:46.370
It's life or death.

00:19:46.370 --> 00:19:49.290
We've been backed into a corner.

00:19:51.920 --> 00:19:53.560
It's beautiful.

00:19:53.560 --> 00:19:56.050
Yes. I'm sure it will be.

00:20:00.300 --> 00:20:02.470
The pork! It's burned...

00:20:02.470 --> 00:20:04.600
I've ruined it all!

00:20:04.600 --> 00:20:06.850
I guess I kept the temperature too high...

00:20:06.850 --> 00:20:08.350
I have returned.

00:20:08.350 --> 00:20:10.640
Uh, welcome back!

00:20:10.640 --> 00:20:13.060
The vinegar. This errand is complete.

00:20:14.110 --> 00:20:15.880
Thank you...

00:20:15.880 --> 00:20:20.340
But now, we've got the sour but no pork!

00:20:20.340 --> 00:20:23.070
Go run another errand for me!

00:20:23.070 --> 00:20:25.570
This time, for pork!

00:20:26.330 --> 00:20:27.440
Pork...

00:20:27.440 --> 00:20:29.320
Learning Mode: "Pork."

00:20:29.320 --> 00:20:31.100
Data acquisition complete.

00:20:31.100 --> 00:20:34.060
Once wild boars, now long since domesticated.

00:20:34.080 --> 00:20:37.220
Some say they were cultivated in Japan during the Yayoi Period,

00:20:37.220 --> 00:20:39.300
and that their numbers grew during the Meiji Period thanks to pig farms.

00:20:39.300 --> 00:20:41.540
They then came to be regarded as a food source.

00:20:41.540 --> 00:20:45.400
Pork is currently the number one meat in Japan.

00:20:45.400 --> 00:20:49.660
It is extremely high in Vitamin B1,
containing ten times more than beef.

00:20:49.660 --> 00:20:55.100
As such, it has restorative properties,
and is widely regarded as an aid against summer fatigue.

00:20:55.100 --> 00:20:58.360
Subroutine "Errand" - Resume.

00:20:58.360 --> 00:21:02.780
Pork can be cheaply obtained at supermarkets and the like,

00:21:02.780 --> 00:21:04.410
but three-breed hybrids such as

00:21:04.410 --> 00:21:06.410
black hog and Iberico pork

00:21:06.410 --> 00:21:09.950
are notable and highly prized, being fed strict diets of...

00:21:10.480 --> 00:21:14.080
They'll soon show up at your door,

00:21:14.080 --> 00:21:19.480
for my special someone, parts of hearts!

00:21:24.120 --> 00:21:29.760
Counting the days I can't see you,

00:21:30.950 --> 00:21:37.210
I want to hear your voice so badly I feel like crying!

00:21:37.210 --> 00:21:40.700
I'm new to this world,

00:21:40.700 --> 00:21:44.170
so I lack the language to describe it.

00:21:44.170 --> 00:21:46.440
To knockoffs, say...

00:21:46.440 --> 00:21:49.890
"No!" Take care to avoid them.

00:21:49.890 --> 00:21:53.410
I want to be be dedicated!

00:21:56.800 --> 00:22:02.110
I want to build it all from nothing!

00:22:02.110 --> 00:22:05.340
We laugh and we fight,

00:22:05.340 --> 00:22:08.950
creating our unique specs!

00:22:08.950 --> 00:22:14.870
By mixing love and hate,

00:22:14.870 --> 00:22:22.940
I want to create more of these funny, carefree days, the parts of Girl!

00:22:39.920 --> 00:22:42.300
Learning Mode: Next episode preview.

00:22:42.300 --> 00:22:46.930
In the forthcoming Frame Arms Girl, Architect, having been blindfolded, shall come to see-

00:22:46.930 --> 00:22:47.970
That's no kind of summary at all!

00:22:47.970 --> 00:22:48.680
